### 1. New category (expect 201, slug "accessories")
POST http://localhost:3000/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Accessories"
}

### 2. Different name, same slug as "Men's Shoes" (expect 201, slug "mens-shoes-2")
POST http://localhost:3000/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mens Shoes"
}

### 3. Rename keeps the slug (use the id from test 1; expect slug still "accessories")
PATCH http://localhost:3000/categories/7
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bags & Accessories"
}

### 4. Change the slug on purpose (same id; expect slug "bags-accessories")
PATCH http://localhost:3000/categories/7
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "slug": "Bags Accessories"
}

### 5. Duplicate name still blocked (expect 409 "Category name already exists")
POST http://localhost:3000/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Evening Wear"
}

### 6. Name without letters or digits (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:3000/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "???"
}